cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use openproceedings in a systematic review or other research, please cite it as below. Save each
  search as a search record and report the record's link, its index_version and the openproceedings release
  (`op --version`): a saved record keeps its index from being retired, so the search can be replayed.
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-05
title: "openproceedings: exact, reproducible Boolean search over NeurIPS, ICLR and ICML titles and abstracts"
abstract: >-
  openproceedings is exact, reproducible Boolean search over the titles and abstracts of NeurIPS, ICLR and
  ICML papers, built for systematic reviews. A query matches only on exact normalized tokens (no stemming or
  synonyms), filters live in the query string, default track and status filters report how many records they
  exclude, and every result set is pinned to an immutable index_version, so a saved search record replays to
  the same ids while its pinned index is served. Exports (RIS, CSV, BibTeX, JSONL) name each abstract's source.
authors:
  - given-names: Jeevan
    family-names: Parmar
    affiliation: "University of Waterloo, SHARE Lab"
  - given-names: Sharon
    family-names: Ferguson
    affiliation: "University of Waterloo, SHARE Lab"
repository-code: "https://github.com/uw-share-lab/openproceedings"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - systematic review
  - boolean search
  - information retrieval
  - reproducibility
  - NeurIPS
  - ICLR
  - ICML
